What is Log Ingestion?
Log Ingestion is the process of collecting logs from different sources, processing them through a pipeline, and sending them to a storage system for analysis and visualization. It is a key part of centralized logging in modern DevOps and cloud environments.

🔹 Log Ingestion Pipeline
A log ingestion pipeline ensures that logs are collected, transformed if needed, and delivered to the right destination.

🔹 Data Flow
Applications / Servers
 │
 ▼
 Log Collectors
(Filebeat / Fluentd)
 │
 ▼
 Logstash
(Filter & Transform)
 │
 ▼
 Elasticsearch
(Store & Index)
 │
 ▼
